Fixed. The effect never cleared its timer, so a pending `setDebounced` could fire after unmount. It now returns a cleanup:

```ts
const id = setTimeout(() => setDebounced(value), delayMs);
return () => clearTimeout(id);
```

This also stops a stale value from landing when `value` changes faster than `delayMs`. Lint is clean and the `useDebouncedValue` tests pass.

